     "explanation": "Beginners burn out during Part 1 (clearing) and Part 2 (updating) because those feel like chores. They quit before reaching Part 3. But long-term practitioners consistently report that **Part 3 — Get Creative — is where the highest-leverage thinking happens**: deciding which someday-maybes graduate to projects, noticing which life domains have no active commitments, and the unscheduled free brainstorm. The maintenance in Parts 1 and 2 buys you the cleared mental space to think strategically in Part 3.",
