     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: Write Your One-Page Implementation Manifesto",
     "content": "On one sheet of paper (or one short doc), write your personal GTD implementation manifesto. It should fit on one page. Include: (1) **My stack:** the four tools you committed to in Practice 1. (2) **My contexts:** the list of @contexts you'll use. (3) **My Areas of Focus:** the 8-15 standing roles from Lesson 7. (4) **My Weekly Review slot:** day and time. (5) **My capture tools by context:** which tool covers desk, meetings, commute, shower, bed, errands. (6) **My top three personal pitfalls to watch for:** pick three from the Top 10 list that you know are your particular vulnerabilities. (7) **My promise to myself for the next 6 weeks:** one sentence committing to no tool-switching, no skipped Weekly Reviews without recovery, no moralizing about slip-ups. Sign and date the page. Pin it visibly. **This document is your contract with the version of yourself who will be living GTD on day 90.**",
